---
permalink: /tour/index.html
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
stages:
  - title: Set up
    blurb: Install Rastrillo, make the app, and run it and its tests.
    from: 1
    to: 4
  - title: Rooms and an admin
    blurb: Give rooms a table, add an admin only admins can open, and list the rooms.
    from: 5
    to: 9
  - title: Live chat
    blurb: Post messages, make every open window show them at once, test it and ship it.
    from: 10
    to: 14
---
{#
  🤖 /tour/: what the tour builds, shown working, then its steps in
  three stages and the way in. The two windows in the hero are the
  finished app's room page drawn in markup: a message sent in Bob's
  arrives in Ada's too, which is what step 11 makes happen. With
  reduced motion they show the end state, still.
#}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark">
<title>{{ tour.title }} · Rastrillo tour</title>
<meta name="description" content="Go from an empty folder to a live chat app, one step at a time.">
<link rel="preload" href="/fonts/ibarra-real-nova.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
<link rel="preload" href="/fonts/chivo.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
<link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/tour.css">
</head>
<body class="tour-index">
{% include "tour-top.njk" %}
{% set first = tour.steps[0] %}
{% set last = tour.steps | last %}
<main class="index">
  <section class="index-hero" aria-labelledby="index-h">
    <div class="index-pitch">
      <h1 id="index-h">{{ tour.title }}</h1>
      <p class="lede"><span class="ai" title="Written by an LLM">🤖</span> Go from an empty folder to a chat app where a message shows up in every open window the moment it is sent. You type every line, and each step tells you how to check it worked.</p>
      <p class="index-go">
        <a class="btn primary" href="{{ first.url }}">Start the tour<svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"/></svg></a>
        {% if last.zipUrl %}<a class="btn" href="{{ last.zipUrl }}" download><svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M21 15v4a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-4"/><path d="m7 10 5 5 5-5"/><path d="M12 15V3"/></svg>Download the finished app (.zip)</a>{% endif %}
      </p>
      <p class="needs">You need Go 1.26 or newer, on Linux, macOS or Windows with WSL. {{ tour.total }} steps, built on Rastrillo {{ tour.version }}.</p>
    </div>
    <figure class="demo" aria-label="Two people in the same room: a message Bob sends appears in Ada's window too.">
      {% for who in ["Ada", "Bob"] %}
      <div class="demo-win demo-{{ who | lower }}" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="demo-bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>{{ who }} · General</span></div>
        <div class="demo-room">
          <p><b>ada</b> Is the new release out?</p>
          <p><b>bob</b> This morning. Try the tour.</p>
          <p class="demo-new"><b>bob</b> Every window gets this at once.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="demo-box"><span class="demo-field"><span class="demo-typed">{% if who == "Bob" %}Every window gets this at once.{% endif %}</span></span><span class="demo-send">Send</span></div>
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
      <figcaption>Step 11 makes this happen: Bob sends, and Ada's window shows it without a reload.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="index-stages" aria-labelledby="stages-h">
    <h2 id="stages-h">The steps</h2>
    <ol class="stages">
      {% for stage in stages %}
      <li class="stage">
        <h3>{{ stage.title }}</h3>
        <p>{{ stage.blurb }}</p>
        <ol class="index-steps">
          {% for s in tour.steps %}{% if s.number >= stage.from and s.number <= stage.to %}
          <li><a href="{{ s.url }}"><span class="n">{{ s.number }}</span><span class="t">{{ s.title | withoutRobot }}</span></a></li>
          {% endif %}{% endfor %}
        </ol>
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ol>
  </section>

  <p class="llm">🤖 These pages were written by an LLM, on the ideas, instruction, and editing of humans. AI-written text here is always marked, visibly — that's <a href="https://11factor.org/#x">factor X</a>.</p>
</main>
</body>
</html>
